;; Type System Test: laundering a qubit through an UNTYPED binder is not caught
;; EXPECT-MODE: default
;; EXPECT-COMPILE: ok
;; EXPECT-NO-STDERR: was consumed more than once

;; Linear tracking is keyed by NAME, and a name is tracked only where the
;; checker can see a linear type on it. Passing a qubit into an unannotated
;; parameter erases that: `a` below is inferred dynamic, so the clone inside is
;; NOT diagnosed and this program compiles and runs.
;;
;; This is a real hole and it is the same shape that defeats the ownership
;; analyzer's name-keyed move tracking. It is pinned here as an ACCEPT on
;; purpose: the fixture records what the compiler does today, so the day
;; place-keyed tracking lands (ADR-0004 PlaceId/FlowEnv) this file must be
;; changed to a reject -- deliberately, by someone who reads this comment --
;; rather than the gap being rediscovered by a consumer.
;;
;; Direct aliases ARE caught: see qubit_clone_via_let_alias_test.esk and
;; qubit_clone_via_alias_chain_test.esk.
(define (h (q : Qubit)) : Qubit q)

(define (laundered (q : Qubit))
  ((lambda (a) (cons (h a) (h a))) q))
(display "laundering through an untyped binder is not enforced")
(newline)
